.TH CHK_MXFS 8 "2026-03-10" "MXFS 0.10.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
chk_mxfs \- validate an MXFS-formatted block device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chk_mxfs
.RB [ \-v ]
.I device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chk_mxfs
performs a read-only integrity check on an MXFS-formatted block device.
It validates all on-disk structures without modifying anything, making
it safe to run on a mounted filesystem (though results may be
inconsistent if the filesystem is actively being modified).
.PP
The checker verifies four categories of on-disk structures:
.SS 1. MXFS Superblock
Reads the first 4 KB at offset 0 and validates:
.IP \(bu 3
Magic number (0x5346584D)
.IP \(bu 3
Format version
.IP \(bu 3
CRC32C checksum
.IP \(bu 3
Region offsets and sizes are within device bounds
.IP \(bu 3
Regions do not overlap (super, journal, disklock, XFS data)
.SS 2. Journal Region
Reads the journal superblock and all per-slot headers:
.IP \(bu 3
Journal super magic (0x4D584A4C), version, and CRC32C
.IP \(bu 3
Per-slot header magic and CRC32C
.IP \(bu 3
Reports clean vs dirty slot counts and slot owners
.SS 3. Disklock Region
Reads the heartbeat slots:
.IP \(bu 3
Heartbeat slot magic (0x4D584C4B) for non-empty slots
.IP \(bu 3
Active/inactive status and node IDs
.IP \(bu 3
Reports active vs empty slot counts
.SS 4. XFS Structures
Reads the XFS superblock and per-AG headers:
.IP \(bu 3
XFS superblock magic (0x58465342), CRC32C at offset 224
.IP \(bu 3
Basic geometry sanity (blocksize, agcount, sectsize)
.IP \(bu 3
Per-AG AGF magic (0x58414746), sequence number, CRC32C
.IP \(bu 3
Per-AG AGI magic (0x58414749), sequence number, CRC32C
.IP \(bu 3
Reports filesystem UUID, block count, free blocks, and inode counts
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v
Verbose output.  Show detailed information for each check as it passes,
including per-slot journal status, heartbeat slot details, and XFS
geometry fields.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check an MXFS filesystem:
.PP
.RS
.nf
chk_mxfs /dev/sdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verbose check showing all details:
.PP
.RS
.nf
chk_mxfs -v /dev/sdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sample output (clean filesystem):
.PP
.RS
.nf
chk_mxfs v1.0.0 -- checking /dev/sdb
MXFS super .............. OK  (version=1, device=20.00 GB)
Journal ................. OK  (64 slots, 64 clean, 0 dirty)
Disklock ................ OK  (64 HB slots, 0 active)
XFS superblock .......... OK  (blocksize=4096, agcount=19, fdblocks=4856307)
  UUID: a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890
  AG 0: AGF OK, AGI OK
  AG 1: AGF OK, AGI OK
  ...

chk_mxfs: 0 error(s) found
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed.  The filesystem structures are consistent.
.TP
.B 1
One or more errors were found.  The error count is printed at the end.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid arguments).
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 3
.B chk_mxfs
is strictly read-only.  It never modifies the device.
.IP \(bu 3
The tool is standalone with no libmxfs linkage.  It uses POSIX
.BR pread (2)
for all I/O.
.IP \(bu 3
CRC verification uses the Castagnoli polynomial (CRC32C, 0x82F63B78).
MXFS structures use seed ~0U without complement; XFS structures use
seed ~0U with final complement.
.IP \(bu 3
.B fsck.mxfs
is installed as a symlink to
.B chk_mxfs
to support automatic fsck dispatch from
.BR fstab (5).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/chk_mxfs
The filesystem checker binary.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/fsck.mxfs
Symlink to chk_mxfs for fstab integration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mxfs (5),
.BR mkfs.mxfs (8),
.BR resize_mxfs (8),
.BR fsck (8),
.BR xfs_repair (8)
